      "text": "Role in ED:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " if a PDE inhibitor is ineffective or poorly tolerated: VEDs, intraurethral prostaglandin or intracavernosal injections; injections: papaverine + phentolamine, or PGE1 + papaverine + phentolamine; excess dosing: priapism in ≤ 1% and genital or pelvic pain in ~10%; priapism = a urologic emergency."
